# mb001, the tally-keeper (doc 84 §9.7): the luna table of cty_brock_marshholm, ported. A shepherd at Larkdowns now (the
# table said Reedfold); the neighbour it named is gone, and the Maker is the Bright One.
mantle mb001
state ready
dialect mirebridge
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for cty_brock_marshholm
title the tally-keeper
fits stage=adult|old
traits talk=chatty piety=devout
quirk keeps_a_tally_of_favours_owed
likes dry_weeks
dislikes broken_promises
fears losing_what_he_built
hopes a_full_fold
topics faith +.3 land +.2
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# tends sheep: chatty behind a reserved manner, devout, and careful to mark every favour owed.

words
saying! = A dry week pays every debt | Keep the tally, keep the trust
duck = duck | my reed
oath! = By the dry bank | Reed and rush

rule @flock
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=herder
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Mind the gate, and count the sheep twice. | No wandering now, #duck#; the flock owes us no favours.

scene tally
when concept=talk.smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self
a : A favour's a favour, given at the fold or owed on the road. I keep the tally.
b[friends] : Am I in your book, then?
b : I know you do. You'll have me in it.

scene watching
when concept=talk.faith
does give.opinion / agree
a : The Bright One watches a straight tongue. I try to give no cause to look twice.
b : #agree#. Best way to live.

line greet.return : #greet#, #duck#. Dry feet to you.
line farewell.return : #farewell#, #duck#.
line react.news.new : Well I never. Is that so?
line react.news.known : I heard. The fold hears everything, given time.
line answer.how : Dry, and thankful for it.

dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. I've your last kindness marked, right here.
